  <!-- Skip Link -->
  <main id="main-content" class="seo-page"><div class="seo-answer"><strong>Direct answer:</strong> Specialized consultations at Mind Grace Neuropsychiatric Clinic cover complex cases such as treatment-resistant depression, bipolar disorder, psychosis and neurodevelopmental conditions, led by consultant psychiatrist Dr. Anita Sharma.</div>
<section class="seo-hero"><p class="seo-kicker">Specialized topics</p><h1>Start with a careful assessment of the right service</h1><p class="seo-lead">Some concerns need specialist teams, physical examination, structured rehabilitation, legal processes, or emergency care. Mind Grace can discuss the concern and help identify an appropriate next step.</p><div class="seo-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Describe the enquiry</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/services">See current services</a></div></section><section class="seo-section"><h2>Topics that require individual confirmation</h2><div class="seo-grid"><article class="seo-card"><h3>Addiction and rehabilitation</h3><p>Addiction, substance use, dual-diagnosis, and rehabilitation needs may require a coordinated or specialist service.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Eating and gender-related concerns</h3><p>Eating-disorder or gender-related support should be approached respectfully and may require specialist assessment or referral.</p></article><article class="seo-card"><h3>Forensic and legal matters</h3><p>Forensic assessment, court-ordered therapy, and legal reports have specific requirements and are not assumed to be available.</p></article></div><div class="seo-note"><strong>Qualified availability:</strong> This page is informational. Availability, suitability, clinician scope, and referral options are confirmed case by case.</div></section><section class="seo-section"><h2>Urgent or immediate risk</h2><p>Mind Grace is not an emergency, crisis-intervention, or suicide-prevention service. If there is immediate danger, call 112 or go to the nearest emergency department. <a href="/emergency">See emergency resources</a>.</p></section>    
  <section class="seo-section"><h2>What does “specialized consultation” mean?</h2><p>Some concerns involve more than one clinical question, a complex history, a previous treatment plan or a need for additional assessment. The word “specialized” does not guarantee that every service listed online is available at the clinic. Availability, clinician scope, suitability and referral options must be confirmed for each enquiry. A person’s needs may be better met by a different service or a specialist team elsewhere.</p><p>When contacting Mind Grace, describe the main question in a few words and ask whether the clinic offers the relevant appointment. Avoid sending a detailed case history through a general contact form. The team can explain what information is needed to coordinate a first conversation and whether another service should be contacted.</p><h2>What to clarify before you request an appointment</h2><ul><li>Which clinician would assess the concern, and what is their stated role?</li><li>Is the appointment intended for assessment, treatment planning, follow-up or referral?</li><li>What records or previous treatment details would be useful?</li><li>What are the current fee, appointment duration and likely next steps?</li><li>Does the concern require a service outside the clinic’s current scope?</li></ul><p>Patients may also review <a href="/psychiatry">psychiatry consultations</a>, <a href="/assessments">assessment pathways</a> and <a href="/therapy">therapy services</a>. For substance-use concerns, see the separate <a href="/addiction-substance-use">substance-use information</a>. For children and adolescents, use <a href="/aasha">Aasha’s child-care pathway</a>.</p><h2>How care may be coordinated</h2><p>A care plan may involve one clinician or more than one service depending on the question. If information needs to be shared between professionals, the patient can ask what will be shared and provide consent where required. A clinician may recommend an in-person review, additional assessment, referral or follow-up if a first conversation does not answer the original question.</p><p>Review <a href="/fees">current fees</a>, <a href="/location">directions</a> and <a href="/process">what to expect</a> before booking. A submitted request does not confirm a slot. The clinic contacts you to agree a suitable time. Mind Grace is not an emergency, crisis-intervention or suicide-prevention service. If someone is in immediate danger, call 112 or go to the nearest emergency department; see <a href="/emergency">emergency resources</a>.</p></section></main>
</Layout>
